WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:41.420
[Narrator:] This film presents the neurological
examination of infants in the first week of life.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.920
In most instances the normal responses are
followed by examples

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.980
of various types of abnormality which may
be encountered.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.210
...when remarks seem needed.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.700
This is clearly only one scheme of examination.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.100
The sequence in which the tests are done will
of necessity vary somewhat from baby to baby,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.780
depending on initial state.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.540
In some cases, other examinations not included
here may need to be added.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.700
Secondly, the matter of interpretation is
beyond the scope of a film of this length.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:21.020
In only a few instances are abnormalities
clearly diagnostic or indicative for treatment.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:28.640
Other abnormalities may clearly be deviations
from normal at the time, but may be transient,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.560
and may be followed by entire future normality
of the baby.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:37.280
In many cases, our present state of medical
knowledge does not permit us either

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:43.740
to explain the abnormality or give a prediction
prognostically for the future.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:58.440
[Narrator:] Many items of examination must be evaluated by observation of the infant at rest,

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.600
preferably with minimal handling.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.760
The head is observed for the position of the
eyes at rest.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.800
Spontaneous movements of the face are observed,
and the palpebral fissures checked

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.060
for width and equality.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.280
One abnormality to be looked for is the setting
sun sign.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:30.380
As in this case of kernicterus, which consists of the [?] appearing to set beneath the lower lid,

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.060
so that white sclera may be seen between the
iris and the upper lid.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.800
Unequal palpebral fissures may be the most
obvious physical sign of facial paralysis,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.640
if the infant is not actively moving the face.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.420
This example is a rather drowsy infant with
neonatal meningitis.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:15.819
The Marcus Gunn phenomenon consists of congenital
ptosis, in which the lid

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.020
is automatically elevated each time the jaw
is moved in sucking.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.980
Spontaneous movements of the body as a whole
and of the limbs are observed.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.700
The character of the movements and the range
of motion of the joints should be appraised.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.220
One should look for possible abnormal movements,
including tremulousness,

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.300
spontaneous writhing movement, myoclonus,
or convulsions.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.940
In Werdnig Hoffman disease the baby is flaccid
and areflexic.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.880
Respirations show bulging of the abdomen and
refraction of the chest.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:05.300
Birth injury of the spinal cord superficially
resembles Werdnig Hoffman Disease.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.219
The abnormal posture of the arms is the most
obvious difference, aside from other responses

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.060
to be demonstrated later.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:22.820
The posture of the arms alongside the head is often one of the most initially striking features of mongolism.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:49.760
Irregular jerking, writhing movements are
characteristic of many normal premature infants.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.440
The earliest observed fetal activity is often
athetotic in nature.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.400
And this type of movement appears to persist
for a time after premature birth.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:11.280
Jittery, tremulous activity may be seen spontaneously
or may be obtained in response

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.940
to almost any stimulus.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.820
Handling, sound, light, or eliciting the moro
reflex

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.300
may show the tremulous movements.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:37.320
Unlike jitteriness, myoclonus is always an
abnormal spontaneous movement.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.160
In this example the pathologic basis is obscured.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.880
Although the infant was subsequently microcephalic,
with spastic diplegia,

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:51.700
the baby remained fully conscious and had
a normal electroencephalogram.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.680
This is an example of convulsive movements
in an unconscious baby

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.380
with abnormal electroencephalogram.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.900
Neonatal convulsions are usually based on
trauma or anoxia at birth,

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.980
or on chemical abnormalities.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:22.440
The causation in this case is obscure, but
the disease was familial and presumably metabolic,

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.400
although no abnormal substance could be identified
in the urine.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:42.420
Abnormal posture of the left arm is obvious
in this case of brachial palsy.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:51.460
However, it is not complete, as some movement
can be obtained in response to pinprick.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:16.980
The blink reflex to light is tested with a
Welch Allyn light or a strong flashlight.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.420
Blinking should be obtained even if the baby's
eyes are closed, unless the baby is crying,

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.640
so that the eyes are already held maximally
closed.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:34.640
An absent blink reflex seldom indicates blindness,
cortical or ocular.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:39.480
More often, as in this example, it is due
to general depression of the central nervous system.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.580
from anesthesia, anoxia or other causes.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.020
Response to sound is tested with a wooden
clacker.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:59.840
The response obtained may consist of a blink,
a startled jump, or a moro reflex.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:05.800
This response is particularly hard to obtain
in many instances and should be repeated

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.320
before one concludes that it is missing.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:19.630
Palmar grasping is tested by applying the
examiner's finger firmly against the palm

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.100
of the hand from the ulnar side.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:38.800
The Palmar grasp response may be absent for
a variety of reasons,

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.300
including Werdnig Hoffman disease, as in this
example.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:52.020
Plantar grasp is similarly tested,

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:56.600
applying the finger to the sole of the foot
near the base of the toes.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:07.820
The knee jerk is the only tendon reflex of
major clinical value in most newborns.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:12.420
It is tested in the conventional manner, but
the head should be in the midline

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.200
at the time of testing.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.200
The knee jerk may be absent, as in this case
of Werdnig Hoffman disease,

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:29.300
or from central nervous system depression,
due to anoxia or other causes.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.960
An exaggerated knee jerk is seen in this baby
with myoclonus.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:46.600
Ankle clonus is best tested by pushing lightly
against the sole of the foot,

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.000
the entire leg being free in the air.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.900
Often none is obtained, but a considerable
number of beats may be elicited

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.720
in many normal infants.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:59.120
The average number of beats obtained should
be recorded.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:21.800
This baby shows ankle clonus, which is sustained
for 8 or 10 beats,

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.620
but nevertheless turned out to be entirely
normal.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:40.420
Slower, more vigorous ankle clonus of greater amplitude is sustained indefinitely in this baby

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.400
with generalized myoclonus.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:56.060
The rooting response is tested by touching
each corner of the mouth and the upper and lower lip in the midline.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:00.840
The infant's head will normally follow in
each direction, but sometimes movement

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.440
of the face and tongue only is obtained.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:09.400
This reflex may be reinforced by previous
testing of the sucking reflex if necessary.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:17.460
Sucking is tested with the examiner's finger
in the infant's mouth,

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.420
the finger being covered with a fingertop
for sterility.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:35.680
An absent rooting response and very feeble
sucking are seen in this case

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:38.140
of congenital Werdnig Hoffman disease.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:57.180
Another case of Werdnig Hoffman disease still
active with incomplete atrophy

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.960
shows a visibly fasciculating tongue.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:05.060
The fasciculation is often most easily seen
on the undersurface of the tongue.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:15.040
Normally, when an infant is picked up and
placed in the prone position with the head in the midline,

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:20.800
the baby will lift up its chin, turn the head
to one side, and make crawling movements with the feet,

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.560
and sometimes with the hands as well.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.960
The arm may be extended on the side toward
which the head turns.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:53.420
Vertical eye movements may be evaluated by
moving the head upward or downward.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.440
The eyes tend to remain fixed toward the examiner,
in a manner rather like

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.120
the eyes of a doll.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:11.860
To test the lobefin reflex the examiner holds
the baby vertically facing him

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:16.200
and turns first in one direction, then in
the other.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:27.140
The effect can best be illustrated with the
research apparatus,

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:31.040
which rotates baby and camera together at
the same speed.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:50.460
During rotation the baby looks ahead in the
direction of rotation.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:01.240
On stopping, the infant looks back in the
opposite direction.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.240
Sometimes only forced deviation of the eyes
is seen.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:09.680
But nystagmus is usually observed in vigorous
mature infants.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:31.800
Reptonic neck reflex is tested by turning
the child's head slowly to the right or left,

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.320
and maintaining it in this position for about
half a minute.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.920
The shoulders should be kept horizontal.

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:44.340
A positive response consists of extension
of the arm and leg on the side toward which

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:47.980
the jaw is turned and flexion of the opposite
limbs.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:51.440
There may be pelvic rotation in addition.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:56.640
No constant pattern is obtained in the majority
of newborns, whether normal or not.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.860
This baby, who subsequently turned out to
be entirely normal, shows fairly consistent

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.040
tonic neck reflexes, particularly in the legs.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:28.300
Even these are not obtained on every occasion
however, and repeated rotation

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.280
of the head is necessary to evaluate the response.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:59.600
This drawing illustrates a strong obligatory
response which the infant

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.560
cannot overcome by struggling.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.860
This is abnormal at any age.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:28.060
The traction response is tested by lifting
the infant from the supine position by pulling on his arms.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.460
There should be assistance from the baby's
shoulder muscles, which can be felt

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.120
by the examiner.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:49.400
When the infant is nearly to the sitting position,
the head should be brought forward and there

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:49.900
should be

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:54.740
sufficient tone in the neck muscles to keep
it from dangling helplessly against the chest

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.260
at the end of the test.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:09.340
The traction response may be absent for a
variety of reasons,

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.180
as in this case of congenital Werdnig Hoffman
disease.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.880
In mongolism the traction response is also
missing.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:26.860
The universal hypertonia becomes evident in
testing this response.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:41.460
An asymmetric traction response, absent on
the paralyzed side,

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.320
is seen in a left-sided brachial palsy.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:06.100
The withdrawal response is tested by applying
a pin to the sole of the foot.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:12.200
Facial evidence of pain should also be looked for, as failure to withdraw the stimulated limb

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.620
may be due to either anesthesia or paralysis.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:22.140
The pin should be applied rather forcefully,
as a gentle pinprick may elicit a response of extension

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.880
rather than withdrawal.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:34.620
This baby with Werdnig Hoffman disease shows
no withdrawal to pinprick.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.280
But there's clear evidence of pain in the
facial expression.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:56.240
An automatic jerky withdrawal is seen in this
baby with spinal cord injury.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:05.400
There is no evidence of appreciation of pain
until the upper level of anesthesia is reached.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:14.260
A striking crossed extension reflex in the
opposite limb may be seen

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.920
in many cases of spinal cord injury.

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.000
The tonic neck reflex may modify crossed extension.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:45.700
Automatic withdrawal and lack of appreciation of pain are clear in this other case of cord injury.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:51.880
The suggestion of crossed extension is only
obtained when the infant is supported

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.500
in the upright posture.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:12.360
Spontaneous stepping movements may be obtained
in most infants if one supports them erect,

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:17.419
placing the soles of the feet firm on the
surface and inclining the trunk and head forward,

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:20.020
or intermittently from side to side.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:29.320
Most mature infants show these stepping movements
at one time or another,

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.200
but not on every occasion.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:43.820
To test the placing response, the infant is
again supported in the erect position and the dorsum

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:49.120
of first one foot and then the other is drawn
upward against the undersurface of the table edge.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:55.100
The baby should lift its foot upward and place
it firmly on the table surface.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:10.220
The placing reflex is poor and feeble in this
baby, but he is quite normal except for being fatigued.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.380
from a long examination.

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.960
The placing response was vigorous on another
occasion.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:22.000
The trunk incurvation reflex can be tested
by stroking the paravertebral areas.

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:36.500
It can also be evoked by pinching the skin
just above the pelvic brim.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:45.200
The moro response can be tested in a variety
of ways, but is most reliable and most complete

00:21:45.210 --> 00:21:50.179
when elicited by supporting the baby under
back and head, and letting the head drop back

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.660
about 30 degrees.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:56.100
Normally the arms first extend and then flex.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.940
The femora also flex on the pelvis in most
cases.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:11.080
An absent moro reflex may be due to Werdnig
Hoffman disease

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:14.400
or more often to depression of the central
nervous system.

00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:27.260
An abnormal stiff type of moro is seen in
kernicterus.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:41.720
Brachial palsy produces an asymmetric moro.

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:45.180
In this example, the paralysis is on the left.

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:50.520
The right arm produces a normal moro response,
while the left arm fails to participate.

00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:59.620
The tone of the neck, trunk, and limbs has
been evaluated during the previous examinations.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:02.820
It may be tested further by manipulation of
the limbs.

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:21.880
[The baby's limbs are extended to examine
the way he reacts.]

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:28.779
The baby should also be suspended in the supine,
lateral, and prone position

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:30.620
on the examiner's hand.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:49.980
Opisthotonos, as in this case of kernicterus,
is best appreciated in the milder cases

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:55.340
if the baby is placed on its side and attention
directed at retraction of the head.

00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:00.000
In more severe cases there may be hypertonus
in all postures.

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:13.000
Universal hypotonia is one of the most striking
signs of mongolism in the newborn.

00:24:32.480 --> 00:24:37.340
Congenital contractures and limitations of
motion are striking in this case

00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:40.440
of arthrogryposis multiplex congenita.

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:45.040
This baby also has club feet, which are treated
by strapping.

00:25:08.300 --> 00:25:13.360
Completely flaccid legs with absent movement
are seen with myelomeningocele.

00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:23.700
Trans-illumination of the head should be carried
out in total darkness with a strong flashlight

00:25:23.700 --> 00:25:25.620
fitted with a light-tight seal.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:32.000
One should attempt to trans-illuminate from
occipit to forehead, against the baby's forehead

00:25:32.620 --> 00:25:34.120
and from side to side.

00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:40.580
With a flashlight in any of these positions,
but especially anteriorly,

00:25:41.040 --> 00:25:46.400
a faint glowing subcutaneous halo around the
circumference of the flashlight is normal.

00:25:46.960 --> 00:25:52.000
Larger, irregular, and brighter areas may
show the presence of an abnormality

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:54.360
and indicate further testing.

00:25:57.880 --> 00:26:04.300
Side-to-side or back-to-front trans- illumination
when seen from the side opposite the flashlight,

00:26:04.300 --> 00:26:08.060
may appear as a total glowing over the entire
head.

00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:12.740
Such an extended area is usually due to hydroencephaly.

00:26:13.340 --> 00:26:16.680
A normal head, of course, will transmit no
light at all.

00:26:21.900 --> 00:26:26.600
The reaction of the pupils to light should
be tested, noting the size of the pupils

00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:30.200
before the light is turned on, and the speed
of constriction.

00:26:36.360 --> 00:26:41.360
A congenital cataract usually appears as an
obvious opacity in the lens,

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:44.260
although there are several possible forms.

00:26:53.620 --> 00:26:59.680
Ophthalmoscopic examination is begun by inspection
of the pupil, cornea, and lens.

00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:04.400
And followed by examination of the eye grounds
in the conventional manner.

00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:10.160
Mydriatic drops are required for adequate
observation,

00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:13.700
and the assistance of a nurse is usually needed.

00:27:16.420 --> 00:27:19.600
If the examination has been done as part of
a collaborative study

00:27:19.610 --> 00:27:24.490
of the National Institutes of Health, the
last two items on the forum concern conditions

00:27:24.490 --> 00:27:26.080
during examination

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:27.780
and opinion as to normality.

00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:32.920
That condition has met...the examiner's opinion,
whether or not a satisfactory examination

00:27:32.920 --> 00:27:34.700
of this baby was obtained.

00:27:36.440 --> 00:27:41.200
The diagnosis is an overall clinical impression
of normality or abnormality.

00:27:42.280 --> 00:27:46.760
If a baby is believed normal, in spite of
certain deviations from the usual findings,

00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:49.260
these may be indicated in the right-hand column.

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:56.380
Finally, if a diagnosis of abnormality is
based on inability to obtain an expected response

00:27:56.380 --> 00:28:01.760
normally present, one should clearly repeat
the observation at the end of the examination,

00:28:01.760 --> 00:28:06.200
or preferably on another occasion before concluding
that it cannot be obtained.

